 "result_text": "`DefFrame` now supports `CHANNEL-DELAY`. I ran one check, parsing a frame definition with `CHANNEL-DELAY: 1e-7`. The attribute showed up as `channel_delay=1e-07` on the `DefFrame`, and `out()` printed it back. I didn't run the test suite.\n\n- **Parsing:** the grammar accepts `CHANNEL-DELAY` as a frame attribute, and the parser maps it to `channel_delay` (`pyquil/_parser/grammar.lark`, `pyquil/_parser/parser.py`).\n- **Construction:** `DefFrame` has a new optional `channel_delay` field, placed after `enable_raw_capture` (`pyquil/quilbase.py`).\n- **Stringification:** `DefFrame.out()` writes `CHANNEL-DELAY` when it's set.\n\nI also added `CHANNEL-DELAY` to the keyword list in `quilbase.py` that sits next to `INITIAL-FREQUENCY`, to match how that attribute is handled. The docstring describes the value as a delay in seconds. I assumed the unit, and it isn't confirmed anywhere in the repo.",
